    choices: [['Which offer gives a specific contribution?', 'I can research the historical background.', 'I will somehow do whatever is necessary.', 'A'], ['What is their agreed route?', 'Gifu, then Kyoto.', 'Fukui, then Gifu.', 'B'], ['How can Haru help?', 'By drawing on his workshop experience.', 'By speaking for every artisan in Japan.', 'A'], ['Which focus follows the grandmother’s advice?', 'Only traditions that have already disappeared.', 'People actively keeping traditions alive.', 'B']],
    mission: { situation: 'You are Aiko. Your tutor is Daniel. During the video call, discuss his invitation. You can research history, Haru has workshop experience, and Mei wants to explore food traditions. The group plans to visit Fukui before Gifu.', task: 'Respond to the proposal, agree on contributions, and explain the people-focused approach.', roles: ['Daniel', 'Aiko'], lines: ['Aiko, would you join me on a documentary journey?', 'Which part of the research would you like to take on?', 'What experience could Haru contribute?', 'Where could Mei’s interest fit into the project?', 'Shall we begin in Fukui before going to Gifu?', 'How should we use Grandmother’s advice when planning the film?'], evidence: 'The reference confirms an invitation and agreement to travel, not a signed production contract, payment, detailed schedule or permission from all future interviewees. Keep the earlier festival successful without claiming the Chapter 1 film was released. Aiko history, Mei food interests, Haru firsthand craft experience, Daniel filming. Grandmother’s advice is about living practitioners. Do not invent a romance or a declining craft as the predetermined conclusion.', useful: ['I would like to propose ...', 'I could take on ...', 'We could draw on ...', 'What if we ...?', 'Our focus should be ...'] },
    topics: [['COLLABORATION', ['How do you match a task to someone’s strengths?', 'What should you ask before volunteering a friend?', 'How can you check that a responsibility is manageable?']], ['PROJECT IDEAS', ['What makes a proposal easy to discuss?', 'How can a group narrow its focus?', 'Why should a project begin with questions?']], ['LEARNING FROM PEOPLE', ['What can a practitioner explain that an object cannot?', 'How can a visitor avoid assuming too much?', 'What would you ask before filming someone’s work?']]],
